title: "HackMatch — US-029: Authenticator Enrollment and Activation Sequence"
---
%%{init: {"theme":"base","themeVariables":{"background":"#ffffff","primaryTextColor":"#1f2937","lineColor":"#4b5563","actorBkg":"#e8f1ff","actorBorder":"#3b82f6","actorTextColor":"#172554","signalColor":"#374151","signalTextColor":"#1f2937","noteBkgColor":"#f3f4f6","noteBorderColor":"#6b7280","noteTextColor":"#1f2937","activationBkgColor":"#eef4ff","activationBorderColor":"#5b8def","labelBoxBkgColor":"#f9fafb","labelBoxBorderColor":"#9ca3af","labelTextColor":"#1f2937","fontFamily":"Arial, sans-serif"},"sequence":{"useMaxWidth":true,"wrap":true,"diagramMarginX":24,"diagramMarginY":18,"actorMargin":30,"width":155,"height":60,"boxMargin":8,"messageMargin":24,"noteMargin":10}}}%%
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Owner as PART or ADMIN owner
    participant React as React authenticator card
    participant API as Express authenticator API
    participant Guards as Auth, MFA, role, and recent-auth guards
    participant Provider as Enrollment provider (AES-GCM, TOTP)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL via Supabase

    Owner->>React: Open account security settings
    React->>API: GET authenticator status
    API->>Guards: Verify token, active account, current MFA, role, recent sign-in
    alt Sign-in older than 10 minutes
        Guards-->>React: 401 reauthentication required, no-store
        React-->>Owner: Offer Verify identity (reauthentication sequence)
    else Authorized owner
        Guards->>Provider: Use resolved participant only
        Provider->>DB: Read status columns only
        DB-->>Provider: Not enrolled, pending, or active
        Provider-->>React: Secret-free status with email OTP fallback
    end

    Owner->>React: Set up authenticator app
    React->>API: POST enrollment with empty body
    API->>Guards: Same guards, then reject any account-targeting field
    Guards->>Provider: Begin for resolved owner
    Provider->>Provider: Generate and encrypt secret
    Provider->>DB: begin_authenticator_enrollment
    DB->>DB: Lock owner, store Pending
    alt Already active or still pending
        DB-->>Provider: Deterministic conflict
        Provider-->>React: 409 already active or pending
    else Pending created with 10-minute expiry
        DB-->>Provider: Enrollment id and expiry
        Provider-->>React: 201 one-time QR URI and manual key
        React-->>Owner: Show QR, manual key, and code input from memory
    end

    Owner->>React: Enter 6-digit code from the app
    React->>API: POST enrollment confirmation
    API->>Guards: Same guards, exactly 6 digits
    Guards->>Provider: Confirm for resolved owner
    Provider->>DB: Read owner-scoped enrollment row
    alt Missing, foreign, canceled, expired, or wrong code
        Provider-->>React: Safe 409, 410, or 401 without secrets
        React-->>Owner: Show error, keep setup unless stale or expired
    else Code valid for current or adjacent 30-second step
        Provider->>DB: activate_authenticator_enrollment
        DB->>DB: Recheck, mark Active
        DB-->>Provider: Activation time
        Provider-->>React: 200 active status, no setup material
        React->>React: Clear setup from memory
        React-->>Owner: Authenticator active, email codes still available
    end

    Note over React,Guards: Foreign enrollment ids receive the same response as nonexistent ids. ADMIN has no cross-account bypass.
    Note over Provider,DB: Only AES-256-GCM ciphertext is stored. The key stays in the server environment, and decrypted secrets exist only during confirmation.
